---
/**
 * The front page, authored in the CMS as an Astro file.
 *
 * This is the source stored in the `pages` entry with slug `index`. It is content
 * only: the build wraps it in the layout version the page selects (`article`) and
 * that layout renders the site's chrome — the navigation bar and the footer bar,
 * both shared components — so this file never repeats them. Edit it in
 * Admin → Content → Pages.
 */
const highlights = [
  { href: '/docs/', label: 'Documentation', hint: 'Guides, fundamentals and package references' },
  { href: '/demos', label: 'Demos', hint: 'Example projects built with ARWES' },
  { href: 'https://arwes-blog.pages.dev/', label: 'Blog', hint: 'Notes on how this site and its CMS work' }
]
---

<p>
  ARWES is a web framework to build user interfaces based on futuristic science fiction designs,
  animations, and sound effects. The concepts behind are opinionated with influences from
  Cyberprep and productions like Star Citizen, Halo, NIKKE, and Mecha Break.
</p>

<ul class="flex flex-col gap-3">
  {
    highlights.map((item) => (
      <li class="flex flex-col">
        <a class="text-secondary-low-2 hover:text-secondary-high-3" href={item.href}>
          {item.label}
        </a>
        <span class="text-primary-low-2 text-size-9">{item.hint}</span>
      </li>
    ))
  }
</ul>

<p class="text-primary-low-2 text-size-9">
  Content only: the frame comes from the CMS layout, the navigation bar and the footer from the CMS
  components.
</p>
